LanguageData.RM_BurnApproachLetter:
{0}

Everything left on open ground burns when it passes: food, wood, crops, bedding. Walls and a roof keep it out. Grass carries it; cut the grass around what you want to keep, or pave a strip, and put your stores indoors.

What it leaves is worth having: for a few days the fresh ash feeds a crop as water would, and scorch-fruit cracks open in the scar, for about a day.
